N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): No source plate exists because this is a new composition; the draft's opening pickup, its mid-tune pickup bar and its overlong bar 9 were removed by rewriting. Bar-by-bar audit, every bar ten eighths (five quarters): bar 1 quarter, two eighths, quarter, half (E A B C5 E5); bar 2 quarter, two eighths, quarter, dotted-quarter rest, eighth "and" (D5 C A F, E); bar 3 five quarters (E G# B E5 B); bar 4 quarter, two eighths, quarter, half rest (E5 C B A); bar 5 triplet D F A, quarter D5, quarter rest, triplet D F A, quarter C5; bar 6 triplet E A C5, quarter E5, two eighths D5 C, half A; bar 7 triplet D F A, quarter D5, two eighths C5 A, half B (Dm for beats 1-3, E for 4-5); bar 8 quarter, two eighths, quarter, half rest (G# A B E); each triplet is three eighths in the time of two, one quarter, so bars 5-7 also total five quarters; bars 9-11 repeat bars 1-3; bar 12 three quarters and a half (E5 D5 B, A). Ostinato: quarter notes root, fifth, fifth, root, fifth on each chord, ending on a half-note A3. Melody pitch set D-E-F-G#-A-B-C-D-E, range D4-E5; leaps are thirds and perfect fourths except where the B section's triplet arpeggio restarts: the octave D5 down to D4 after the rest in bar 5 and the minor sixth C5 down to E4 into bar 6; ostinato range A3-B4. Form ABA'. Originality check: the opening E-A-B-C-E rise, the counting bar and the triplet arpeggios were compared with "Take Five" (melody, vamp and later lyric) and with common counting songs; no shared hook was found; arpeggios and a root-fifth ostinato are common property.
N:UNCERTAIN: Whether Grade 6 singers keep the 3+2 grouping steady with the ostinato at quarter = 104, whether the triplets are clean, whether the E5s suit the class and how the page's pop band plays 5/4 can only be settled by a classroom trial. The originality check is one reader's; a second score reader should repeat it. The authorized link is the Brubeck estate's official page for Time Out, which names the album and year; it does not itself play the track.
